# Portfolio content integrity

- Never invent or infer personal accomplishments.
- Do not create fake metrics such as percentages, revenue, user counts, performance improvements, or team sizes.
- Do not change employment dates, employer names, job titles, education, project status, or technical claims unless repository evidence supports the change or the owner explicitly supplies the information.
- Do not replace contact information because it looks unusual.
- Improve grammar, clarity, scanning, and information hierarchy without altering factual meaning.
- When consolidating duplicated project data, preserve the most complete repository-supported version and surface conflicts for review.
- If a link is broken, do not silently substitute a guessed URL.
- Placeholder images may be replaced only with real repository assets or owner-provided assets; do not invent project screenshots.
